.TH MACOSX-CROSS 1 "September 2026" "macosx-cross @MACOSX_CROSS_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
macosx-cross \- manage macOS SDKs and cross-compilation tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B macosx-cross
.RB [ \-s | \-\-silent ]
.I command
.RB [ options ]
.RI [ SDK_VERSION ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B macosx-cross
manages macOS SDK installations and provides access to the tools installed
by the macosx-cross package.

It can install, remove, reinstall, and refresh macOS SDKs, list available
SDKs, remove cached SDK archives, and copy installed tools into the current
directory.

The
.B \-s
or
.B \-\-silent
option must appear before the command and suppresses normal informational
output. Errors are still displayed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent
Enable silent mode.

.TP
.B \-y
Skip confirmation prompts for commands that remove or reinstall SDKs.

.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display the macosx-cross version and exit.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Install one or more macOS SDK versions.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross install 14.5
macosx-cross install 14.5 15.5
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B reinstall
Remove and reinstall one or more macOS SDK versions.

By default, confirmation is required.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross reinstall 14.5
macosx-cross reinstall 14.5 15.5
macosx-cross reinstall -y 14.5
macosx-cross reinstall -y 14.5 15.5
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B refresh
Refresh the metadata and extraction state of one or more installed SDKs.

This does not reinstall the SDK archive.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross refresh 14.5
macosx-cross refresh 14.5 15.5
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B allrefresh
Refresh every installed macOS SDK.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross allrefresh
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B remove
Remove one or more installed macOS SDKs.

By default, confirmation is required.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross remove 14.5
macosx-cross remove 14.5 15.5
macosx-cross remove -y 14.5
macosx-cross remove -y 14.5 15.5
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B uninstall
Alias for
.B remove.

.TP
.B allremove
Remove every installed macOS SDK.

By default, confirmation is required.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross allremove
macosx-cross allremove -y
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B list
List the available macOS SDKs.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross list
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B clean
Remove cached SDK archives.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross clean
.fi
.RE

.TP
.BR \-\-tool =TOOL
Copy an installed tool directory into the current directory.

The copied directory is changed to be owned by the invoking user.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross --tool=cmake
.fi
.RE

.TP
.BR \-\-tool " " TOOL
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-tool =TOOL.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross --tool cmake
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B \-\-list-tool
List the installed tools.

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross --list-tool
.fi
.RE
.SH SILENT MODE
Silent mode can be enabled with
.B \-s
or
.BR \-\-silent .
The option must appear before the command.

For example:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross -s allrefresh
macosx-cross --silent install 14.5 15.5
.fi
.RE

Silent mode suppresses informational messages generated by
.B macosx-cross
and its SDK management scripts where supported. Errors are not suppressed.

Note that
.B sudo -s
is a sudo shell option and is unrelated to the
.B macosx-cross
.B \-\-silent
option.

.SH EXAMPLES
Install an SDK:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross install 14.5
.fi
.RE

Install multiple SDKs:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross install 14.5 15.5
.fi
.RE

Refresh an installed SDK:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross refresh 15.5
.fi
.RE

Refresh all installed SDKs:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross allrefresh
.fi
.RE

Remove an SDK without confirmation:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross remove -y 14.5
.fi
.RE

Reinstall an SDK without confirmation:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross reinstall -y 15.5
.fi
.RE

Remove all installed SDKs:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross allremove -y
.fi
.RE

List available SDKs:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross list
.fi
.RE

Copy an installed tool:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross --tool cmake
.fi
.RE

List installed tools:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross --list-tool
.fi
.RE

Run silently:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross -s allrefresh
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@
macosx-cross installation root.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk
Installed macOS SDK directory.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/cache
Cached macOS SDK archives.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/scripts
SDK management scripts.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/tools
Installed cross-compilation tools.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.

.TP
.B 1
An error occurred, an invalid command or argument was supplied, or an
operation was cancelled.
